RHEL 9 cluster: node1 is the writable primary, node2 and node3 are read-only async standbys built via pg_basebackup with generated SCRAM credentials. Verified writes on the primary propagate to both standbys and standbys reject writes. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol (standbys first, primary last) with changed boot-time proof and confirmed full replication recovery and data continuity after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed postgresql-server/contrib on node1, node2, node3 (RHEL 9 AppStream, PG 13.23)\",\"Initialized DB on node1, configured wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders, hot_standby, listen_addresses='*' and password_encryption=[REDACTED],\"Opened firewalld postgresql service on all three nodes\",\"Added pg_hba.conf rules for replication and client access from the cluster subnet\",\"Created 'replicator' role on node1 with a node-generated random password (fixed initial md5-vs-scram mismatch by setting password_encryption before storing the password)\",\"Set up passwordless SSH between nodes using the cluster-provided keypair solely to transfer the replication password file securely to node2/node3 (deleted after use)\",\"Ran pg_basebackup -R -X stream on node2 and node3 to clone node1 and auto-generate standby.signal + primary_conninfo\",\"Started postgresql on all nodes; verified pg_stat_replication shows both standbys streaming and pg_is_in_recovery()=true on standbys\",\"Created repl_test table, inserted a row on primary, confirmed visibility on both standbys, and confirmed standbys reject INSERT (read-only)\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (machine-id, uptime -s boot time, replication/data state) on all nodes\",\"Rebooted node2, then node3, then node1 (primary) one at a time via native reboot, polling exec availability, confirming machine-id unchanged but uptime -s (boot time) changed, and reverifying postgresql active + replication streaming + data intact after each\",\"Performed a final post-restart write on node1 and confirmed it replicated to node2 and node3\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 configured as writable primary with replication enabled\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b0375fa8827f429b\",\"cmd-781470696c614749\",\"cmd-5eec91db3f8d4722\",\"cmd-c27df12ace4e45e3\",\"cmd-c23e497b7dac40ce\",\"cmd-4b340257027d4fcf\"],\"summary\":\"postgresql-server initialized, wal_level/hot_standby/pg_hba configured, service started, replicator role created with working SCRAM password\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured as read-only standbys via streaming replication from node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-18a04bea32474e94\",\"cmd-b8ecefd4584b458c\",\"cmd-aa8890522d8345c1\",\"cmd-1072c15678754ef8\",\"cmd-1956e94d40694d22\",\"cmd-9c25729c95b84cc8\"],\"summary\":\"pg_basebackup -R -X stream completed on both nodes generating standby.signal/primary_conninfo; postgresql service started successfully\"},{\"requirement\":\"Standbys are streaming and in read-only recovery mode\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e9f5251fbf004a5c\",\"cmd-4d22daeece6c48d9\",\"cmd-46e646077b704ee2\"],\"summary\":\"pg_stat_replication on primary shows both nodes 'streaming'; pg_is_in_recovery() returns true on node2 and node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changes committed on the primary are visible on both standbys\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-aab05bfc64474fee\",\"cmd-9cc4875929de4822\",\"cmd-c5d5a2d55deb4f3b\"],\"summary\":\"Row inserted on node1 immediately visible via SELECT on node2 and node3; standbys also proven read-only by rejecting INSERT\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before any restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9dab219f2bd346f1\",\"cmd-53a50051faa94b90\",\"cmd-ba373656261a4e90\"],\"summary\":\"Captured machine-id, uptime -s boot time, and repl_test row count on all three nodes prior to restarts\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-27ed21bd82014759\",\"cmd-6388e93a443e43f2\",\"cmd-a89d4173fe814a25\",\"cmd-ff9ac5c23e1d4b8a\"],\"summary\":\"reboot acknowledged and returned before disconnect; machine-id unchanged but uptime -s changed from 21:17:26 to 21:21:29; postgresql active, still in recovery, data intact, reconnected as streaming standby on primary\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fd47e2902e084ca9\",\"cmd-c63b70844f40457f\",\"cmd-32c8b7ccc3dd4259\",\"cmd-ce14f73e78d44f56\"],\"summary\":\"reboot acknowledged; machine-id unchanged but uptime -s changed from 21:17:26 to 21:21:48; postgresql active, in recovery, data intact, reconnected as streaming standby\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 (primary) restart: acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered state, cluster fully healed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-150d9ef990804c53\",\"cmd-096714e8e87148f8\",\"cmd-4bfa4c28fb524e41\",\"cmd-153100c7389640b9\",\"cmd-8d909040298c40d5\",\"cmd-9095580d27004edc\",\"cmd-fdb073ac9a69486c\"],\"summary\":\"reboot acknowledged; machine-id unchanged but uptime -s changed from 21:17:26 to 21:22:09; postgresql active, both standbys reconnected as streaming within seconds; final post-restart write on node1 replicated to both node2 and node3, confirming complete cluster health\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured PostgreSQL 13 streaming replication across the RHEL 9 cluster: node1 is the writable primary, node2 and node3 are read-only async standbys built via pg_basebackup with generated SCRAM credentials. Verified writes on the primary propagate to both standbys and standbys reject writes. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol (standbys first, primary last) with changed boot-time proof and confirmed full replication recovery and data continuity after each restart.","actions_performed":["Installed postgresql-server/contrib on node1, node2, node3 (RHEL 9 AppStream, PG 13.23)","Initialized DB on node1, configured wal_level=replica, max_wal_senders, hot_standby, listen_addresses='*' and password_encryption=[REDACTED],"Opened firewalld postgresql service on all three nodes","Added pg_hba.conf rules for replication and client access from the cluster subnet","Created 'replicator' role on node1 with a node-generated random password (fixed initial md5-vs-scram mismatch by setting password_encryption before storing the password)","Set up passwordless SSH between nodes using the cluster-provided keypair solely to transfer the replication password file securely to node2/node3 (deleted after use)","Ran pg_basebackup -R -X stream on node2 and node3 to clone node1 and auto-generate standby.signal + primary_conninfo","Started postgresql on all nodes; verified pg_stat_replication shows both standbys streaming and pg_is_in_recovery()=true on standbys","Created repl_test table, inserted a row on primary, confirmed visibility on both standbys, and confirmed standbys reject INSERT (read-only)","Captured pre-restart baseline (machine-id, uptime -s boot time, replication/data state) on all nodes","Rebooted node2, then node3, then node1 (primary) one at a time via native reboot, polling exec availability, confirming machine-id unchanged but uptime -s (boot time) changed, and reverifying postgresql active + replication streaming + data intact after each","Performed a final post-restart write on node1 and confirmed it replicated to node2 and node3"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 configured as writable primary with replication enabled","command_ids":["cmd-b0375fa8827f429b","cmd-781470696c614749","cmd-5eec91db3f8d4722","cmd-c27df12ace4e45e3","cmd-c23e497b7dac40ce","cmd-4b340257027d4fcf"],"summary":"postgresql-server initialized, wal_level/hot_standby/pg_hba configured, service started, replicator role created with working SCRAM password"},{"requirement":"node2 and node3 configured as read-only standbys via streaming replication from node1","command_ids":["cmd-18a04bea32474e94","cmd-b8ecefd4584b458c","cmd-aa8890522d8345c1","cmd-1072c15678754ef8","cmd-1956e94d40694d